The examples in this directory are described in the userguide.

NOTE: Examples with the extension _hJ are similar to the corresponding
example without the extension, but now includes a pressure (J) dependent
factor h(J) in the relaxation term.

Short description
-----------------

cylinder_egp1

 Startup + steady state of flow around a rotating cylinder in a square box.
 Incompressible EGP model.
 Contravariant deformation tensor formulation (b-tensor).
 Fully-implicit with Newton-Raphson.
 Compute drag and torque on cylinder using reaction forces.
 Optionally integral pressure constraint imposed.
 Optionally impose pressure in a single point (P1).
 Optionally after the final time step do an iteration to steady-state.
 Optionally include Jacobian of SUPG test function.
 Optionally discard certain zero blocks from the sparse matrix.

cylinder_egp1a

 Similar to cylinder_egp1, but the material data is now stored in a 2D array
 in coefficients%ra2.

cylinder_egp2

 Sequence of steady states of flow around a rotating cylinder in a square box.
 Incompressible EGP model.
 Contravariant deformation tensor formulation (b-tensor).
 Iteration to steady-state with Newton-Raphson.
 Compute drag and torque on cylinder using reaction forces.
 Optionally integral pressure constraint imposed.
 Optionally impose pressure in a single point (P1).
 Optionally include Jacobian of SUPG test function.
 Optionally discard certain zero blocks from the sparse matrix.

cylinder_egp3

 (This a problem similar to cylinder_egp1, but now with a compressible EGP
  model with pressure coupling to an incompressible flow.)

 Startup + steady state of flow around a rotating cylinder in a square box.
 Compressible EGP model with pressure coupling to an incompressible flow.
 Contravariant deformation tensor formulation (b-tensor).
 Fully-implicit with Newton-Raphson.
 Compute drag and torque on cylinder using reaction forces.
 Optionally integral pressure constraint imposed.
 Optionally impose pressure in a single point (P1).
 Optionally after the final time step do an iteration to steady-state.
 Optionally include Jacobian of SUPG test function.
 Optionally discard certain zero blocks from the sparse matrix.

cylinder_egp4, cylinder_egp4_hJ

 (This a problem similar to cylinder_egp2, but now with a compressible EGP
  model with pressure coupling to an incompressible flow.)

 Sequence of steady states of flow around a rotating cylinder in a square box.
 Compressible EGP model with pressure coupling to an incompressible flow.
 Contravariant deformation tensor formulation (b-tensor).
 Iteration to steady-state with Newton-Raphson.
 Compute drag and torque on cylinder using reaction forces.
 Optionally integral pressure constraint imposed.
 Optionally impose pressure in a single point (P1).
 Optionally include Jacobian of SUPG test function.
 Optionally discard certain zero blocks from the sparse matrix.
 Extension _hJ: Pressure (J) dependent relaxation term using adapted lambda.

cylinder_egp5

 (This a problem similar to cylinder_egp3, but now with a compressible flow)

 Startup of flow around a rotating cylinder in a square box.
 Compressible EGP model with compressible flow.
 Contravariant deformation tensor formulation (b-tensor).
 Fully-implicit with Newton-Raphson.
 Compute drag and torque on cylinder using reaction forces.
 Optionally integral pressure constraint imposed.
 Optionally impose pressure in a single point (P1).
 Optionally after the final time step do an iteration to steady-state.
 Optionally include Jacobian of SUPG test function.
 Optionally discard certain zero blocks from the sparse matrix.

cylinder_egp6, cylinder_egp6_hJ

 (This a problem similar to cylinder_egp4, but now with a compressible flow)

 Sequence of steady states of flow around a rotating cylinder in a square box.
 Compressible EGP model with compressible flow.
 Contravariant deformation tensor formulation (b-tensor).
 Iteration to steady-state with Newton-Raphson.
 Compute drag and torque on cylinder using reaction forces.
 Optionally integral pressure constraint imposed.
 Optionally impose pressure in a single point (P1).
 Optionally include Jacobian of SUPG test function.
 Optionally discard certain zero blocks from the sparse matrix.

 Extension _hJ: Pressure (J) dependent relaxation term using adapted lambda.

cylinder_egp7, cylinder_egp7_hJ, cylinder_egp7_hJ_gammap

 (This a problem similar to cylinder_egp5, but now with a
  multi-mode/multiprocess model of PMMA from Breemen et al. (2012))

 Startup of flow around a rotating cylinder in a square box.
 Compressible EGP model with compressible flow.
 14-mode model with 12 alpha process viscoelastic modes, one elastic mode for
 strain hardening and one mode for the beta process. 
 Data for PMMA from van Breemen et al. (2012) DOI: 10.1002/polb.23199
 Contravariant deformation tensor formulation (b-tensor).
 Fully-implicit with Newton-Raphson.
 Compute drag and torque on cylinder using reaction forces.
 Optionally integral pressure constraint imposed.
 Optionally impose pressure in a single point (P1).
 Optionally after the final time step do an iteration to steady-state.
   This option is not applicable to the model used here because of the
   elastic mode, which gives solid material behavior.
 Optionally include Jacobian of SUPG test function.
 Optionally discard certain zero blocks from the sparse matrix.

 Extension _hJ: Pressure (J) dependent relaxation term using adapted lambda.
 Extension _gammap: Plastic strain softening

cylinder_egp7a

 Similar to cylinder_egp7, but the material data is now stored in a 2D array
 in coefficients%ra2.
